{%- comment -%}
  The index behind the finder (assets/js/keys.js) and the 404's suggestions.

  Fetched once, on the first keystroke that needs it, and then cached by the
  browser — so it costs nothing on a visit that never opens the finder. That is
  why it is a file and not inlined into every page.

  Keys are one letter because this ships to every reader who opens the finder
  and the whole point is that it stays small. Roughly 200 bytes per post.

    t  title          u  url            c  category
    g  tags           d  date           x  excerpt, for context under the row

  Every value goes through `jsonify`, which quotes and escapes it. A title with
  a quote or a backslash in it is the reason — building JSON by hand with
  string concatenation works right up until someone writes about `"` parsing.
{%- endcomment -%}
[
{%- for post in site.posts -%}
{%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless -%}
{"t":{{ post.title | jsonify }},
"u":{{ post.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
"c":{{ post.categories.first | default: "" | jsonify }},
"g":{{ post.tags | jsonify }},
"d":{{ post.date | date: "%Y-%m-%d" | jsonify }},
"x":{{ post.excerpt | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | strip | truncate: 160 | jsonify }}}
{%- endfor -%}
]
